     <th><para unique="1091394">Instruction</para>
      </th>
     <th><para unique="1091396">Op/ En</para>
      </th>
     <th><para unique="1091398">64-Bit Mode</para>
      </th>
     <th><para unique="1091400">Compat/&#8232;Leg Mode</para>
      </th>
     <th><para unique="1091402">Description</para>
      </th>
     </tr>
    </thead><col width="98.25984pt"/>
   <col width="111.46464pt"/>
   <col width="24.767999999999997pt"/>
   <col width="48.024pt"/>
   <col width="46.728pt"/>
   <col width="180.65448pt"/>
   <tbody>
    <tr>
     <td><para unique="1091404">F6 /4</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1091406">MUL r/m8<footnote><para unique="1092122" format="TableFootnote"><anchor id="70102: TableFootnote: 1. With a REX prefix in 64-bit mode, attempts to acce"/>With a REX prefix in 64-bit mode, attempts to access AH, BH, CH, or DH will instead access SPL, DIL, BPL, or SIL, respectively.</para>
        </footnote></para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1091408">M</para>
      </td>
